# What never enters the image build.
#
# The Dockerfile's build stage does `COPY . .`, so everything in this directory
# ships to the builder unless it is named here. Three kinds of things must not:
#
#   Secrets and state. A checkout used for local development carries a database
#   with a live Dispatcharr credential in its settings, .env files, and editor
#   swap buffers beside the compose file. None of it has any business in a
#   builder layer, which is retained by the registry's build cache and scanned
#   by trivy like any other input.
#
#   Host build output. A host node_modules or .next copied over the ones the
#   deps stage installed and the build stage produced would quietly replace
#   container-built artefacts with machine-specific ones -- the native
#   better-sqlite3 binding is the case that actually breaks, but none of it is
#   honest to ship.
#
#   Weight. .git and the docs images are most of this directory; excluding them
#   keeps the build context small enough that cache hits dominate build time.

# Version control and CI machinery
.git
.github
.forgejo
.woodpecker
.ci
.gitignore
.gitleaksignore
.trivyignore
renovate.json
cliff.toml

# Host dependencies and build output
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Local state: the dev database carries a live Dispatcharr credential, and an
# exported config can carry one too.
data/
.env
.env.local
.local/

# Editor and agent scratch state
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Documentation and release metadata: nothing here is read by `next build` or
# the esbuild worker bundle, and docs/images is the largest tree after .git.
docs/
*.md
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
